  "description": "Take one part plus bike, one part mountain bike, and one part cruiser and whaddya get? This bike. And it's splendid because you get the gearing of a mountain bike, the supple ride of a plus bike, and the easygoing simplicity of a cruiser. Did we intend that from the start with the Railer Plus? Well, the jury's still out on the one my friend, but one thing's for sure: it's a winning combo, intentional or otherwise, so we'll take it.\nWide, high-rise BMX-inspired handlebars provide comfort, laid-back positioning, and stylistic stability\nSupple 26+ tires and wide rims smooth out bumps and provide float in sandy conditions\n8-speed gearing adds versatility to a laid-back cruiser making the Railer Plus equally adept at climbing hills to the beach overlook or blasting down the bike path\nPedal-forward positioning allows for full leg extension while still easily putting a foot down at stop signs",
